## olap vs oltp
- untraceable: OLAP and OLTP serve different purposes.
- untraceable: OLTP systems are designed for transactional workloads, handling high rates of read and write operations on individual records  .
- untraceable: In contrast, OLAP systems are built for running large analytics queries, often involving scanning large volumes of data  .
- untraceable: OLAP systems are less efficient for individual record lookups  .
- untraceable: Both types of systems are important in data management, with OLTP supporting real-time transactions and OLAP enabling scalable analytics  .
